:: OC Kalim Water Polo Training [nobr]

/* Intro */
As you walk along the edge of the pool, you notice that a large section of it, about a third, is sectioned off from the rest with a red and white floating barrier. Inside the sectioned off area is a group of about half a dozen or so high schoolers seemingly practicing laps. You can even feel the speed and intensity of their practice from here. Though you wonder why they are practicing here rather than at their school? <br>
<br>
<<if $Player.Kinks.Teens == 1>>
    Though you only think about that for a second, since as they exit the water to take a break, <span style="color:Pink">you notice how every single one of them wears nothing but a small, purple speedo. You feel your face flush, the small bit of clothing leaving next to nothing to the imagination. Their bulge is perfectly noticeable, even from here, and the way some ride up their rears causes you to heat up. Swimmer’s really do have near perfect physical form!</span> <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

Amongst the group, you notice one which you recognize. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span>, the musical prodigy that you met at school. <span style="color:LightGreen">He leaps into the water and, like a blur, he takes off! He moves faster than all the others, seemingly born to swim. He reaches the end even faster than someone running alongside him would! You find yourself impressed and can’t look away as he surfaces, the shimmering wetness causing the blue patches on his body to shine. You feel a bit bad for staring but can’t look away.</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Kalim",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Speedo",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>
/* OC Kalim: Speedo, Smile */

<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> gets praise and compliments from his teammates, some saying that he is impossible fast and others making jokes about him <span style="color:LightBlue">“being slower than usual.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> just seems to laugh it off, taking a moment at the edge of the pool to catch his breath. Then he spots you staring in the distance and waves, <span style="color:LightGreen">smiling in a way that seems to make your heart flutter strangely.</span> <span style="color:Pink">You quickly turn red and spin around.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightBlue">“Hey, I’ll be right back guys. Need a breather.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> says climbing out of the pool in one well practiced movement, the water cascading off their body could be heard even from here. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightBlue">“Yeah, hurry back. You need the practice!”</span> One of them says sarcastically as they continue their drills. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> walks up behind you and pats you on the back, causing you to jump. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightBlue">“Haha, sorry.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> gives you a smile, the same one that made your heart flutter again. 

<<if $Player.Kinks.Teens == 1>>
    <span style="color:Pink">Your mind instantly turns to mush as you see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span>, in just his tiny speedo, standing right in front of you with his body shining from the water, their abdomen tensing each time they breathed making their already impressive muscles stand out more. You really hope your groin isn’t obvious in your $PlayerBottoms.Type.</span> 
<</if>>

<span style="color:LightBlue">“Good to see you. How you doing?”</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "OC Kalim",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Speedo",
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>
/* OC Kalim: Speedo, Smile
PC: Smile */

You greet him, unable to resist complimenting his skills in the water. <span style="color:LightBlue">“Oh, it’s nothing. I’ve just had a lot of practice. Anyone would be that good with the time I’ve put into it. Plus, this is just basic laps, you should see when we actually start practicing. Water polo can get pretty intense! Though we like to ease into it.”</span> He laughs, rubbing the back of his head. <span style="color:LightBlue">“In fact, I’m exhausted from that last run. Was going to take 5 on the lounge chairs. Care to join me? I would love to hear how your music practice is going, or whatever else, if you don’t want to talk about that.”</span> <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Sit & chat<br>">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
		You nod, following <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> over to the lounge chairs and sit down. <span style="colorYellow">As he leans back, the light catches the blue scaley patches on his skin. You don’t want to stare, but they look so strange yet enchanting.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> catches you looking and chuckles, turning his back towards you. <span style="color:LightBlue">“Here, want a better view?”</span> <br>
		<br>
		You quickly apologize, claiming the light reflecting off of them just caught your eye, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> just waves it off. <span style="color:LightBlue">“No worries, I don’t mind people staring. Afterall, it is a little weird.”</span> Feeling a little more comfortable, you ask if it hurts. <span style="color:LightBlue">“Nah, not really. I hardly notice them to be honest. It’s a skin condition called Psoriasis.”</span> You try to repeat the word but flub it a few times before jokingly asking why they don’t just call it Scaleoriasis or something. <br>
		<br>
		<span style="color:LightBlue">“Haha, that’s a good one.”</span> <span style="color:Pink"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> laughs at your joke, causing you to smile.</span> <span style="color:LightBlue">“But don’t feel bad about looking or asking about them. I take it as a compliment.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span>’s presence relaxes you and you chat with him for a minute before he gets up to leave, having to return to his practice. <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<needChange "Energy" 7>>
        <<socialChange "Kalim" 3 1>>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <br>
        <<if $PoolLocation == "Very Deep">>
            [[Continue|Pool Very Deep]]
        <<elseif $PoolLocation == "Deep">>
            [[Continue|Pool Deep]]
        <<elseif $PoolLocation == "Part Shallow">>
            [[Continue|Pool Part Shallow]]
        <<else>>
            [[Continue|Pool Shallow]]
        <</if>>
	<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<link "Ask for Swimming pointers<br>">>
	<<replace"#choice">>
		You ask if he actually wouldn’t mind giving you some swimming tips. <span style="color:LightBlue">“Oh? Sure. Music or swimming, I’m a teacher at heart. Let’s see your strokes.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> sits along the edge of the pool as he watches you swimming back and forth a few times. You quickly tire out, slowing down and having to stop to catch your breath. <span style="color:Pink">As you do so, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> suddenly reaches down and plucks you out of the pool.</span> <br>
		<br>
		<span style="color:LightBlue">“Don’t over do it.”</span> He says, carrying you all the way over to the chairs and placing you gently down. You find yourself blushing by the time he takes a seat next to you. <span style="color:LightBlue">“You’re not bad, but you need to work on your control. You went too hard too fast. That’s dangerous. If you pull something or run out of energy in the middle of the pool, you could be in trouble. Wouldn’t want someone to have to come in and save you, would you?”</span> <br>
		<br>
		<<if $Player.Kinks.Teens == 1>>
			<span style="color:Pink">Blushing, you ask if he would have dove in to save you.</span> <span style="color:LightBlue">“Of course, what kind of teacher would I be if I didn’t? Though I think the lifeguards here would have it covered. Still, just because there are people around, doesn’t mean you shouldn’t be safe.”</span> <br>
			<br>
		<<else>>
			You apologize, saying you didn’t realize that and just wanted to show him what you could do. <span style="color:LightBlue">“Well, you still need to be careful. Showing off is fine and all, just make sure you stay safe. Alright?”</span> You nod, taking his advice to heart. <br>
			<br>
		<</if>>
		<span style="color:LightGreen"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kalim</span> spends the next few minutes going over some better stroke and breathing techniques with you. By the end, you feel you’ve learned something!</span> Though you feel a little bad for taking up his whole break, though he doesn’t seem to mind. <span style="color:LightBlue">“No worries, talking with you was more than relaxing. But I should be getting back. Remember what I said, alright?”</span> He gives you a smile before heading off back to his practice. <br>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<needChange "Energy" 7>>
        <<socialChange "Kalim" 3 1>>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<skillPoints "Swimming" 10>>
        <br>
        <<if $PoolLocation == "Very Deep">>
            [[Continue|Pool Very Deep]]
        <<elseif $PoolLocation == "Deep">>
            [[Continue|Pool Deep]]
        <<elseif $PoolLocation == "Part Shallow">>
            [[Continue|Pool Part Shallow]]
        <<else>>
            [[Continue|Pool Shallow]]
        <</if>>
	<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>